From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wispr: detach contexts before freeing their portal

A context retains a borrowed pointer to its shared portal. A context can
outlive the portal's hash-table entry while an asynchronous callback holds a
reference. Clear the backpointers held by the portal slots before dropping
their references, so a later context destructor cannot dereference the freed
portal.

This covers synchronous setup failure for one address family while the other
family has a callback in flight, as well as other portal teardown paths.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/wispr.c
+++ b/src/wispr.c
@@ -417,6 +417,13 @@ static void free_connman_wispr_portal(gpointer data)
 	if (!wispr_portal)
 		return;
 
+	/* Context callbacks may outlive the portal's hash-table entry. */
+	if (wispr_portal->ipv4_context)
+		wispr_portal->ipv4_context->wispr_portal = NULL;
+
+	if (wispr_portal->ipv6_context)
+		wispr_portal->ipv6_context->wispr_portal = NULL;
+
 	wispr_portal_context_unref(wispr_portal->ipv4_context);
 	wispr_portal_context_unref(wispr_portal->ipv6_context);
 
